Funding-Text = {COH remembers that reading Leroi-Gourhan (1975) when he was a student
   was a seminal moment in shaping his decision to become a palynologist.
   In 1992 he met Arlette Leroi-Gorhan and was hugely impressed by her
   detailed and thoughtful discussion of the `Flower Burial'. This paper is
   dedicated to her memory. The paper was written as part of the ongoing
   reassessment of the archaeology of Shanidar Cave, led by Graeme Barker,
   Tim Reynolds and Chris Hunt. We thank the Directorate of Antiquities of
   the Kurdish Regional Government and especially General Directors Mala
   Awat and Kaifi Mustafa Ali, the Director for the Soran District
